me, \"email\": email})\n}\n\nNeed refactor. External behavior identical: status codes, response bodies. Note original success response: Content-Type application/json, body JSON object with name/email plus trailing newline from Encoder. Error responses: no Content-Type set, body exact strings no newline. Need preserve. If we use helper writeJSON? For errors, must not set Content-Type? Original doesn't set Content-Type for errors. If helper sets Content-Type for all, external behavior changes (headers). User says same status codes, same response bodies, not necessarily headers? But likely keep identical external behavior including headers? It says same status codes, same response bodies. Could still set Content-Type on errors? That changes headers, maybe not desired. Better preserve exact: errors write raw bytes no Content-Type. Success sets Content-Type and encodes JSON.\n\nNeed separate database access, input validation, JSON encoding into testable functions. Could define:\ntype user struct { Name, Email string }\nfunc parseUserID(r *http.Request) (int, error) { ... }\nfunc getUser(db *sql.DB, id int) (user, error)", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0009350975160486996], [22916, -7.939108371734619]], [[1144, -1.3709161976294126e-05], [513, -12.072084426879883]], [[4087, -0.009456262923777103], [310, -4.9871344566345215]], [[1156, -0.029826892539858818], [303, -3.7767693996429443]], [[579, -0.3156713843345642], [25, -2.0933451652526855]], [[1622, -0.002924123778939247], [3296, -6.750785827636719]], [[13, -0.42218732833862305], [25, -1.4198031425476074]], [[14235, -0.02879519760608673], [1165, -4.1712188720703125]], [[89109, -0.2778647243976593], [7936, -1.9382022619247437]], [[5805, -0.00020583602599799633], [2400, -8.946334838867188]], [[9830, -0.028318224474787712], [6795, -3.638019323348999]], [[6795, -3.314073182991706e-05], [17369, -11.866820335388184]], [[47781, -1.3813896179199219], [1083, -1.6238842010498047]], [[4475, -1.0028866529464722], [2833, -1.0942354202270508]], [